# --- Hybrid search ---
pref-hybrid-title = Hybrid Search
pref-hybrid-desc = Keyword + semantic retrieval, fused into one 0-1 relevance score. Used both to find literature across the library and to dig into a single document.
pref-hybrid-gpu-label = Activar aceleración vectorial por GPU
pref-hybrid-gpu-hint = Solo tarjetas gráficas NVIDIA; se requiere un controlador NVIDIA compatible.
pref-hybrid-gpu-precision-label = Precisión de cálculo
pref-hybrid-gpu-precision-hint = Auto usa Float32 si hay memoria GPU suficiente; de lo contrario, Int8.
pref-hybrid-gpu-precision-auto = Automática
pref-hybrid-gpu-status-disabled = { $backend } · { $precision }; la aceleración por GPU está desactivada.
pref-hybrid-gpu-status-preparing = Preparando recursos de GPU...
pref-hybrid-gpu-status-loading = { $backend } · { $precision }; cargando vectores ({ $loaded }/{ $total })...
pref-hybrid-gpu-status-available = { $backend } · { $precision }; { $device }, { $vectors } vectores residentes.
pref-hybrid-gpu-status-fallback = { $backend } · { $precision }; GPU no disponible ({ $code }): { $reason }
pref-hybrid-gpu-fallback-notification = La aceleración vectorial por GPU no está disponible; se usa la CPU ({ $code }): { $reason }
pref-hybrid-retrieval-label = Retrieval limits
pref-hybrid-max-documents-label = Max highly relevant documents
pref-hybrid-max-documents-hint = How many documents one library-wide search may return. An upper bound only - weaker matches are never added to fill it.
pref-hybrid-max-chunks-label = Max chunks per document
pref-hybrid-max-chunks-hint = How many passages one document may return when the AI digs into it. Also an upper bound only.
pref-hybrid-min-score-label = Minimum relevance
pref-hybrid-min-score-hint = Anything scoring below this after fusion is discarded, at both levels. Higher = stricter and fewer results, lower = broader and noisier.
pref-hybrid-neighbor-radius-label = Neighbouring chunk expansion
pref-hybrid-neighbor-radius-hint = When a passage lacks context, how many passages either side the AI may pull in. 0 disables expansion.
pref-hybrid-advanced-title = Advanced: chunking (rebuild required)
pref-hybrid-chunk-target-label = Chunk target length
pref-hybrid-chunk-target-hint = How many characters of Markdown paragraphs each passage accumulates before it closes.
pref-hybrid-chunk-tolerance-label = Paragraph append tolerance
pref-hybrid-chunk-tolerance-hint = Once a passage reaches the target, a next paragraph no longer than this still joins it; a longer one starts the next passage.
pref-hybrid-chunk-rebuild-title = Important: after changing the chunk target length or the paragraph append tolerance, the whole-library semantic index must be rebuilt.
pref-hybrid-chunk-rebuild-p1 = These two parameters change where body text is split. The existing index still holds the chunks and vectors produced by the old chunking rules, and they are not converted to the new chunking automatically.
pref-hybrid-chunk-rebuild-p2 = Only after a whole-library rebuild are existing documents re-split under the new chunk rules, re-embedded, and brought back into the current index.
pref-hybrid-chunk-rebuild-p3 = Changing a parameter never triggers a rebuild by itself; the plugin only reports that the index is out of sync, and the whole-library rebuild is yours to run.
pref-hybrid-chunk-stale-warning = The existing semantic index was built with different chunk settings than the ones below. Rebuild the whole-library semantic index with the buttons above so retrieval matches these settings.
pref-hybrid-vector-scan-timeout-label = Tiempo límite de escaneo vectorial (ms)
pref-hybrid-vector-scan-timeout-hint = Tiempo máximo que la rama semántica puede dedicar a escanear el índice. El embedding de consulta tiene su propio límite y no consume este presupuesto.
pref-hybrid-keyword-search-timeout-label = Tiempo límite de búsqueda por palabras clave (ms)
pref-hybrid-keyword-search-timeout-hint = Tiempo máximo para buscar en los metadatos de Zotero. Al agotarse devuelve los resultados ya ordenados en lugar de ninguno.
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-button = Probar escaneo completo
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-hint = Mide ambas ramas sobre tu biblioteca real y rellena un valor recomendado en cada casilla de arriba. Después puedes cambiarlos a mano.
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-running-vector = Ejecutando escaneos vectoriales...
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-running-keyword = Ejecutando búsquedas por palabras clave...
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-result-vector = Escaneo vectorial ({ $runs } ejecuciones sobre { $chunks } fragmentos) — mínimo { $min } ms · promedio { $average } ms · máximo { $max } ms → recomendado { $recommended } ms
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-result-keyword = Búsqueda por palabras clave ({ $runs } ejecuciones por perfil, perfil más lento «{ $profile }») — mínimo { $min } ms · promedio { $average } ms · máximo { $max } ms → recomendado { $recommended } ms
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-result-profile =   · { $profile }: { $min } / { $average } / { $max } ms con { $candidates } candidatos
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-coverage = Medido sobre { $chunks } fragmentos indexados y { $items } elementos muestreados. Si indexas más adelante, repite la prueba: un índice mayor escanea más despacio.
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-error = Falló la prueba de escaneo: { $message }
